UPDATE physim.experiments 
SET overview = 'The Ohm’s Law Virtual Lab is an interactive simulation designed to study the relationship between voltage, current, and resistance in an electrical circuit. The experiment demonstrates one of the fundamental laws of electricity proposed by Georg Simon Ohm. According to Ohm’s Law, the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the applied voltage across it, provided the temperature and physical conditions remain constant.

This virtual laboratory allows students to perform the experiment digitally by adjusting voltage and resistance values, observing the resulting current flow, and analyzing the voltage-current relationship through graphical visualization. The simulation provides a realistic experimental environment without requiring physical laboratory equipment, making it accessible, safe, and repeatable.

The experiment also helps students understand practical applications of electrical circuits, resistor behavior, circuit analysis, and the importance of Ohm’s Law in electrical and electronic engineering systems.'
WHERE slug = 'ohms-law';
